---
import AplusPage from '../../layouts/AplusPage.astro';
---
<AplusPage title="Managed Service Wiki | A+ Active Services" eyebrow="Wiki / managed service" heading="Not every healthcare product starts as pure software." intro="Some of the best prototypes begin as a managed service with automation behind the scenes and human review where it matters.">
  <section class="aplus-screen-stack" aria-label="Managed service operating model">
    <article>
      <p class="aplus-kicker">DWY before DFY</p>
      <h2>Use service delivery to learn what the software should become.</h2>
      <p>The Healthcare Software Factory can start as done-with-you office hours, workflow audits, and back-office automation before we lock the product shape.</p>
    </article>
    <article>
      <p class="aplus-kicker">When to productize</p>
      <h2>Operational metrics decide when a service becomes software.</h2>
      <p>We track repeated questions, handoff time, review burden, payment friction, and calendar follow-through so the build is pulled by evidence instead of vibes.</p>
    </article>
  </section>
  <section class="aplus-flywheel-strip" aria-label="Managed service tools">
    <span>Forms</span>
    <span>Slack</span>
    <span>Calendar</span>
    <span>Payments</span>
    <span>Docs</span>
  </section>
  <section class="aplus-content-grid">
    <article><h2>Package the outcome</h2><p>Sell the result first, then use the build to reduce delivery cost and improve quality.</p></article>
    <article><h2>Automate the back office</h2><p>Use Slack, forms, calendars, payments, and document workflows to remove the repetitive middle.</p></article>
    <article><h2>Know when to productize</h2><p>The retainer helps decide what should become software, service, or a hybrid.</p></article>
  </section>
</AplusPage>
